{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>With seventy souls your fathers went down to Egypt.</b> He says: from the great and awesome deeds that He did with you, you are obligated from this to love Him, for those who went down to Egypt were only seventy, and now you are like the stars of the heavens — and therefore He joined to it: ״ואהבת את ה׳ אלהיך״ — and you shall love HaShem your Elohim — ״ושמרת משמרתו״ — and you shall keep His charge. And the reason He mentioned here 'seventy,' and likewise in the place where He counted them (Genesis 46:27): ״כל הנפש לבית יעקב הבאה מצרימה שבעים״ — all the souls of the house of Jacob who came to Egypt, seventy — yet we find only sixty-nine: our Rabbis of blessed memory already expounded, this is Yocheved, who was born between the walls; and some say this is Serach bat Asher, who completed their count, as it is said (II Samuel 20:19): ״אנכי שלומי אמוני ישראל״ — 'I am the completeness of the faithful of Israel' — I completed the count of Israel. But I have seen in the Pesikta: this is the Holy One, blessed be He, who completed their count, as it is said (Genesis 46:4): ״אנכי ארד עמך מצרימה״ — I will go down with you to Egypt — the Holy One, blessed be He, entered with them in His glory; what is the reason? As it is written: ״הוא תהלתך והוא אלהיך״ — He is your praise and He is your Elohim — and immediately afterward: ״בשבעים נפש״ — with seventy souls — to teach you that the Holy One, blessed be He, entered into the count of the seventy. And according to what they expounded on the verse (Exodus 12:37): ״כשש מאות אלף רגלי״ — about six hundred thousand footmen — that they were one short, for the Holy One, blessed be He, entered with them and completed them to sixty myriads. And if so, behold we find that the Holy One, blessed be He, completed their count both on the going up and on the going down: on the going down, to seventy; on the going up, to sixty myriads; and this is what was said to Jacob (Genesis 46:4): ״אנכי ארד עמך מצרימה ואנכי אעלך גם עלה״ — I will go down with you to Egypt, and I will also surely bring you up."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:24.379767041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}